From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:53:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: s2r: let one bring-up abort still tell
 the enclave

A run with abort_before set no longer sends the enclave its sleep
request. That keeps an aborted run harmless, but it also takes the
request and what follows it out of every run short of a real sleep, and
that is where a refused-path run stopped before.

Add abort_tells_enclave: with abort_before=1, send the request again
before the abort, so that this stop can be reproduced with the
breadcrumb and the bring-up watchdog recording it. It is refused unless
breadcrumb, wdt_from_enter and wdt_timeout are all set and abort_before
is 1.

The parameter is off by default; without it nothing changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c
index 839317d5d2..35a1cccb0a 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c
@@ -586,6 +586,10 @@ static bool breadcrumb;
 module_param(breadcrumb, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(breadcrumb, "For bring-up: during a suspend-to-RAM, write the number of each late step (0x31-0x3d) to the PMU boot stage byte, so that a sleep that never returns leaves its last step for the next boot; the original value is put back once user space is thawed (default: off)");
 
+static bool abort_tells_enclave;
+module_param(abort_tells_enclave, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(abort_tells_enclave, "For bring-up: with abort_before=1, still send the enclave its sleep request before the abort, as before the enclave was left out of aborted runs, to reproduce a stop there under instrumentation; refused unless breadcrumb, wdt_from_enter and wdt_timeout are all set (default: off)");
+
 static char breadcrumb_trail[128];
 module_param_string(breadcrumb_trail, breadcrumb_trail, sizeof(breadcrumb_trail), 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(breadcrumb_trail, "Breadcrumb result of the last suspend-to-RAM cycle: steps written, write errors, value read back at the end, value put back");
@@ -1020,6 +1024,18 @@ static int apple_s2r_enter(suspend_state_t state)
 		return -EBUSY;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Bring-up: an aborted run that still tells the enclave reaches a
+	 * stop no log can report, so only with the breadcrumb and the
+	 * watchdog on, and only aborting before any SoC step.
+	 */
+	if (READ_ONCE(abort_tells_enclave) &&
+	    (READ_ONCE(abort_before) != S2R_STEP_PARKED || !READ_ONCE(breadcrumb) ||
+	     !READ_ONCE(wdt_from_enter) || !READ_ONCE(wdt_timeout) || !s2r->wdt)) {
+		pr_warn("apple-s2r: abort_tells_enclave needs abort_before=1, breadcrumb, wdt_from_enter and wdt_timeout: refused\n");
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	if (!apple_s2r_abort_reachable(s2r, READ_ONCE(abort_before))) {
 		pr_warn("apple-s2r: abort_before=%u is never reached here: refused\n",
 			READ_ONCE(abort_before));
@@ -1069,9 +1085,11 @@ static int apple_s2r_enter(suspend_state_t state)
 	/*
 	 * The coprocessors' last refusals, before anything that can't be undone.
 	 * The enclave's sleep request gates it, and only the power cycle of a
-	 * real sleep brings it back: a run that aborts on purpose doesn't send it.
+	 * real sleep brings it back: a run that aborts on purpose doesn't send it,
+	 * unless abort_tells_enclave asks for exactly that.
 	 */
-	ret = apple_s2r_coprocs_check(s2r, !READ_ONCE(abort_before));
+	ret = apple_s2r_coprocs_check(s2r, !READ_ONCE(abort_before) ||
+				      READ_ONCE(abort_tells_enclave));
 	if (ret) {
 		s2r->failed_step = S2R_STEP_COPROCS;
 		goto fail;
